lines+=['','[OpenMP speed and RSS graph](figures/linux-openmp.png). Four post-matrix stream probes observed **97 native process threads with 96 readers / OpenMP=1**, and **192 with one reader / requested OpenMP=96**, on both backends. These probes are excluded from performance counts. Retained initialization/runtime teams mean the latter does not isolate a single 96-thread pool or SMT effects.','','## RSS and per-reader overhead','','The peak-RSS comparison covers streaming, retained whole loads, fast indexed queries and default metadata-plus-query paths at every reader count. These are whole-process `wait4` peaks including launch/startup. A post-run empty-target calibration measured 11→139 MiB when the Python parent allocated an extra 128 MiB: pre-exec accounting can impose a floor on low-memory cells. Exact per-cell parent RSS was not recorded, so small peaks are not pure parser footprints and differences below the driver floor should not be ranked. Large 96-reader peaks exceed this floor; the in-process retained `statm` samples do not include it. At 96 readers:','','| Input | Path | Xerces peak GiB | Complete libxml2 peak GiB |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
