lines+=['','![Context overhead](figures/linux-context-overhead.png)','','[Context table](linux/context-overhead.csv) retains every count and both resident/peak estimates. Whole-document output data are deliberately retained until all workers finish; their RSS is not a streaming parser footprint.','','## macOS and Timo’s question','','[Controlled macOS results and options](MACOS_OPTIONS.md) separate three effects: encoding, build configuration, and two private source experiments. A local unpatched `-Os` libxml2 build reproduces the installed bottle’s Latin-1 times within 0.1%; `-O2` reduces them about 14% for streaming and 23% for opening, whereas `-O2` versus `-O3` alone makes little difference. Homebrew’s recorded Clang default is `Os`, so formulas and Release labels did not establish the earlier O2/O3 assumption.','','The private converter/ignored-binary combination improves Latin-1 streaming/opening by 23.1%/47.6% versus the Homebrew-backed complete replacement, with about 52/104 MiB RSS. It is **not shipped** in the canonical branch or used in the Linux runs. Under matched native `-O3` builds it still trails Xerces on Latin-1 by 13.7%/16.9%; on UTF-8 the unpatched builds are near parity and the combination opens 13.7% faster. Honest UTF-8 serialization and speed-optimized parser builds are practical options before a wider adapter rewrite.','','![Within-host encoding/build controls across platforms](figures/platform-encoding.png)','','Different CPU, compiler, allocator and Xerces transcoder choices remain confounded across hosts. The paired Linux and macOS declaration controls isolate encoding effects on this ASCII-body input; they do not justify blind header changes to real Latin-1 files.','','## Evidence and limits','','The Xerces Linux rebuild passed all 25 focused XML tests; the complete replacement passed all 28, each benchmark correctness suite, and million-point stream/load/index equivalence; the full replacement’s source/library dependency guard passed. Every final measured cell has five records and matching decoded fingerprints; library hashes and input hashes are checked before/after. The actual source archives and benchmark executable are pinned. The broader 747-test Linux validation remains available in the parent migration report.','','The private macOS converter passed all eight native suites per build, 51,472 oracle cases and 65 exact in-place ASCII cases; the combined handler candidate passed 12 focused OpenMS tests and 24 malformed/non-ASCII payload controls. Independent Kimi/Opus reviews and the Codex caller review are retained. Native Xerces’s one upstream DOM baseURI-test failure also reproduces with the installed bottle; it is disclosed rather than counted as passing. Windows, Docker and sanitizers were not newly run.','','Raw matrices, summaries, hashes, resource/load/swap observations and reproduction scripts are included. All 62 copied Linux result/log files passed transport checksum verification before the successful dedicated task-owned scratch root was removed; shared contrib was preserved. The [cleanup receipt](linux/cleanup.json) records the outcome. The resource log shows at least 880 GiB available and unchanged swap-in/out counters throughout the timed matrices.']
